  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Pampelonne is a long beach of fine sand, 4.5 km, classified as a remarkable natural area and the origin of the "Saint-Tropez myth": people swim, eat and party there, according to the Ramatuelle tourist office page. For a quiet swim in season, the tourist office advises coming in the morning before 10am or in the evening after 7pm; car parks are free before 11am and after 5pm.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The Ramatuelle tourist office states (FAQ and 2025 "Dog friendly" leaflet) that all the town's beaches — Pampelonne bay, the Bonne Terrasse cove, L'Escalet beach and the Canadel coves — are open to dogs kept on a leash; swimming is allowed except in the ZRUB (zones reserved solely for bathing). No time slot is announced.</p>
      <p>The Pampelonne beach police regulation (2021, article 16) specifies: dogs may only walk on the beach on a leash; from 1 April to 15 October they are banned, even on a leash, in the zones reserved solely for bathers, but tolerated on a leash in the zones closed to motorised craft. Letting a dog foul the beach is forbidden (pick up after it). Category 2 dogs must be muzzled and held on a leash by an adult. To find out where the bathers-only zones are, the tourist office leaflet refers to the lifeguard posts: ask them.</p>
      <p>Other useful points: the tourist office page (updated on 06/02/2026) states that dogs are allowed, kept on a leash, all year round, and that the beach is supervised, with free access, car parking, showers, toilets and food. The beach is reached by several entrances (route de Bonne Terrasse, chemin de Garonne, boulevard Patch, chemin des Tamaris, chemin des Moulins, route de Tahiti). On the coastal path, dogs on a leash are tolerated, as long as they stay on the path. Var Tourisme also mentions dog showers for rinsing dogs on some of the town's beaches, such as L'Escalet.</p>
      <p><strong>Worth checking before you go:</strong> the regulation currently in force (the text read dates from 2021; the commune's recent orders concern noise and pollution), the location of the bathers-only zones, and each beach establishment's own rules.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: on a 4.5 km beach, move away from the immediate surroundings of the beach establishments, often crowded, to leave room for your dog and others.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The coastal path leads to the Bonne Terrasse cove at the south of the bay, then to L'Escalet beach and Cap Taillat. The hilltop village of Ramatuelle rounds off the outing.</p>
